# Test fixture 04 — invented property names must fail.
#
# Per spec §2.2: "the per-glass qualifier set isn't just a list of
# strings. It's a list of refs into the chain, each backed by
# `literal`'s name-IS-operation discipline. A glass that binds
# `property foobar` fails at compile time because
# @epistemologic/property/foobar does not resolve — `literal(foobar)`
# returns `fail(no_such_property)`."
#
# This locks down the grounding discipline. New property names cannot
# be invented at the glass altitude; they must already exist in the
# canonical chain (or below `---` as named conjunctions of chain
# primitives — see fixture 08).
#
# Expected: parse OK; resolve FAILS with
#           `literal(foobar): @epistemologic/property/foobar does not resolve`.

in @io

grammar @test/04/invented {
  glass to @io {
    property foobar    # not in the chain; not defined below ---;
                       # therefore: invented; therefore: compile error.
  }
}
